[info] StableIdsSpec:
[info] - frozen formula values match an independent implementation
[info] - IDs are deterministic across calls
[info] - run IDs ignore input order but change with attempt, code, config, and inputs
[info] - work IDs are namespace plus authoritative source ID
[info] - researcher ID uses a validated ORCID, else a versioned ScholarChain identity ID
[info] - ORCID checksum is enforced and synthetic fixture IDs are never ORCID iDs
[info] - coauthor edge ID is independent of argument order and depends on window and policy
[info] - graph edge ID canonicalizes undirected endpoints only, and evidence order is ignored
[info] - community ID: frozen value (JOBS.md job 6 formula), shape, and window sensitivity
[info] - chunk ID changes with any of its inputs
[info] - affiliation-name ID: frozen value, canonical form, version, and empty names
[info] - ID parts containing the separator are refused
[info] - canonical pair rule: smaller ID first, self-pairs refused
[info] - query ID: frozen value (RUNTIME.md audit formula), shape, input sensitivity, and guards
[info] - ID format checks accept well-formed and reject malformed IDs
[info] CommunityPathSpec:
[info] ValidationSpec:
[info] - every fixture is valid
[info] - missing provenance is rejected
[info] - incomplete provenance is rejected
[info] - confidence outside [0, 1] is rejected
[info] - unsupported schema versions are rejected, including a nested provenance version
[info] - malformed stable IDs are rejected
[info] - a coauthor edge ID that does not match its formula is rejected
[info] - a synthetic ORCID fixture ID is accepted as a source record ID
[info] - non-canonical and self pairs are rejected
[info] - Community nodes need comm- IDs; MEMBER_OF runs from a researcher to a community
[info] - a pair candidate's mentions must belong to its work
[info] - windows whose start year exceeds the end year are rejected
[info] - evidence bundles keep graph facts and semantic context apart
[info] - supported claims must cite evidence; unsupported claims may not
[info] - match decisions need reason codes and an ISO-8601 timestamp
[info] - a null field is rejected, not thrown
